{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-bmb","title":"Backup: newer 'channel canvas tab' content is never captured (~88% of channels with real canvas content)","description":"Discovered while investigating f3redmond/all-f3-redmond's channel canvas: slackdump's FILE table\nhas zero Canvas rows for that channel despite CHANNEL.properties.canvas.is_empty=false (real\ncontent exists). properties.canvas.file_id is blank - only an opaque canvas-tab id is present\n(e.g. \"Ct0A6BK5B154\" under properties.tabs[].type==\"canvas\"), not a classic Slack file id.\nVerified against the freshest CHANNEL row (today's resume, so not a staleness artifact) -\nslackdump genuinely never resolves a file id for this canvas type, so nothing is ever downloaded:\nno content, no creator, no created/updated timestamps, nothing recoverable locally.\n\nScope, surveyed across all 483 locally archived channels (freshest CHANNEL row vs FILE table):\n- 91 channels: canvas genuinely empty (is_empty: true) - expected, nothing to capture.\n- 19 channels: no canvas property at all.\n- 45 channels: non-empty canvas successfully captured (has file_id + matching FILE row) - e.g.\n  ao-active-book-club, all-announcements. This is the set docs/DESIGN-export.md's \"Files \u0026\n  Canvases\" section and export_logic._load_channel_files were built around.\n- 328 channels: non-empty canvas (is_empty: false) but NO file_id and NO FILE row - content is\n  simply invisible to the whole pipeline (backup, digest, channel-digest). all-f3-redmond is\n  typical of this majority, not an outlier.\n\nThis is a backup-layer capture gap, not an export/digest filtering issue - the recent digest\nwork (images + non-image file content extraction, SlackBackup-qpw) has nothing to fix here since\nthere's no local file at all for these 328 channels' canvases.\n\nWorking hypothesis: Slack has (or this data reflects) a newer \"channel canvas\" product tracked by\na canvas-tab id (Ct...) rather than the older pinned-Canvas-as-classic-File model slackdump's\nfile harvesting (files.info-based) understands. Needs investigation before any fix:\n1. Does slackdump (github.com/rusq/slackdump) have, or plan, direct Canvas API support\n   (canvases.* Slack API methods) independent of the classic files model?\n2. If not, is there a canvas.info-equivalent reachable through slackdump's existing chunk/session\n   auth this project could piggyback on, consistent with the project's constraint of only ever\n   calling the slackdump binary (see docs/DESIGN.md \"This app never talks to the Slack API\n   directly\")?\n3. If slackdump has no path at all, this may be an upstream feature request/wait, not something\n   this project can close itself without breaking its own architecture constraint.\n\nNo content extraction, no digest change, no backup change implemented yet - investigation only\nuntil the above is resolved.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-24T15:19:49Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-24T15:19:49Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-qpw","title":"Digest: surface images and improve non-image file content extraction","description":"Currently _load_channel_files() drops image/* files entirely from channel-level files[], message-attached files[] carries no local_path (no way to find the downloaded blob), and _extract_file_content() only handles text/* and the Canvas HTML mimetype. Add: (1) images included in channel-level files[] with metadata+local_path (no content extraction), (2) message-attached files[] gains local_path, (3) content extraction extended to PDF (pypdf) and docx/pptx (zipfile+regex, stdlib) — xlsx included via a similar approach. Survey of live archives: 46 PDF/docx/pptx files (~31MB) total; 5539 images (12.3GB) currently invisible in digests.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-24T14:51:55Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-24T15:01:00Z","started_at":"2026-07-24T14:52:31Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T15:01:00Z","close_reason":"Implemented: images now included in digest files[] (metadata+local_path, no content), message-attached files[] gains local_path, content extraction extended to PDF (pypdf)/docx/pptx/xlsx (stdlib zipfile+regex). Docs updated (DESIGN.md, DESIGN-export.md). 347 tests pass; verified against real archives (f3cascades/otb-red-eye-reps images+PDFs, f3nation scanned-PDF graceful-None case).","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-0z2","title":"backup run: --workspace/--channel selectors to filter channels.json subset","description":"Add optional --workspace and --channel glob selectors to 'backup run' so a subset of channels.json can be backed up without a hand-filtered channels file or knowing channel IDs. Same comma-separated glob semantics as 'export digest --workspace'. Both selectors AND together; an empty match raises a clear error; omitting both preserves current behavior. Motivation: quick single-workspace/single-channel refresh before regenerating one digest.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-19T02:29:29Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-19T03:06:54Z","started_at":"2026-07-19T02:29:34Z","closed_at":"2026-07-19T03:06:54Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-ccs","title":"bd-run-beads: permission-denial reporting, BLOCKED/HANDOFF protocol, recovery messaging","description":"Follow-on to SlackBackup-daq and SlackBackup-y3l. Make every failure self-describing and give unattended sessions a handoff protocol. Evidence of the gap: /home/stuar/proj/RankChoiceVoting/.bd-run-beads/20260714-024642Z/run.log - the session was denied git commit 6 times, ended saying it would wait for approval (meaningless headless), and the runner reported only \"session ended without closing the bead\". All work is in scripts/bd-run-beads.py and scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh.\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/bd-run-beads.py:\n1. session_prompt(): add a step - if a command is denied for permissions (tool error mentions requires approval) or you are blocked for any other reason, do NOT retry it and do NOT wait; record a handoff by running bd update \u003cid\u003e --notes=\"HANDOFF: \u003cwhat is done\u003e / \u003cwhat remains\u003e / \u003cwhat a human must decide\u003e\", then end your final message with a line starting exactly \"BLOCKED: \u003cone-line reason\u003e\".\n2. run_session(): while streaming, track assistant tool_use blocks (id -\u003e command brief) and detect user tool_result blocks with is_error whose content contains \"requires approval\" (also match the shell-safety rejections such as command_substitution and expansion messages). Log each live to run.log as \"permission denied: \u003ccommand brief\u003e\" and collect the list. Also capture session_id (present on stream events) and the final result text from the result event. Return these alongside the exit code.\n3. Gate: if the final result text contains a line starting \"BLOCKED:\", fail the bead BEFORE committing - leave the tree uncommitted, leave the bead open, and report the BLOCKED reason verbatim.\n4. Every bead-failure path (session rc, test gate, BLOCKED, no-op, close verification) must print a recovery block: bead id and current status; count of staged/unstaged changes from git status --porcelain; each collected permission denial; a resume hint \"claude --resume \u003csession-id\u003e\" for interactive takeover; and a reminder that rerunning the same bd-run-beads command skips closed beads and resumes at this bead.\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh:\n5. Fake claude gains env-triggered modes emitting fabricated stream-json: DENY_ONCE=1 emits an assistant tool_use for a git commit command followed by a user tool_result with is_error true and content \"This command requires approval\", then a normal result; BLOCKED=1 emits a result whose text contains a \"BLOCKED: needs a human decision\" line.\n6. New assertions: run.log contains \"permission denied\" with the command brief; a BLOCKED session fails the bead with the reason echoed, no commit created, bead still open; failure output contains \"claude --resume\" and the rerun-resumes hint.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Denied commands are logged live as \"permission denied: \u003ccommand\u003e\" and echoed in the failure block. 2. A session whose final message contains a BLOCKED: line fails the bead before any commit; the tree is left uncommitted and the bead open, and the reason is echoed. 3. Every bead failure prints bead status, change counts, collected denials, \"claude --resume \u003csession-id\u003e\", and the rerun-resumes note. 4. ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh passes.","notes":"CAUTION: unrelated in-flight work exists in the tree (export/digest files, ADR drafts). Stage ONLY scripts/bd-run-beads.py, scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh, and work-log.md; never git add -A/-u/. Quality gate: ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-14T03:09:56Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-14T03:31:14Z","started_at":"2026-07-14T03:27:20Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T03:31:14Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-ccs","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-y3l","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T20:10:07Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-y3l","title":"bd-run-beads: default --allowedTools for mandated commands; npm test detection","description":"Follow-on to SlackBackup-daq (runner-side commit/close must land first so the session allowlist does not need git commit). All work is in scripts/bd-run-beads.py and scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh.\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/bd-run-beads.py:\n1. --allowed-tools default: when the flag is not given (default None), compute and pass to claude an allowlist covering exactly what the session prompt mandates: Bash(bd:*), Bash(git add:*), Bash(git status:*), Bash(git diff:*), Bash(git log:*), Bash(git rev-parse:*), plus Bash(\u003ctest_cmd\u003e:*) when a test gate is active. A value passed explicitly (including an empty string, which means none) is used verbatim.\n2. detect_test_cmd(): restructure candidates as (command, probe) pairs. New first candidate: when package.json exists, declares scripts.test (parse the JSON), and npm is on PATH (shutil.which), return \"npm test\". The npm probe must NOT execute npm test (that runs the whole suite) - JSON presence plus npm on PATH is the probe. Keep the pytest candidates and their --collect-only probe unchanged, after npm.\n3. Update the module docstring (model cue section unchanged; document the default allowlist and npm detection).\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh:\n4. Fake claude: when env ARGS_DUMP is set, write the value it received for --allowedTools to that path.\n5. New assertions: with no --allowed-tools flag the dumped value contains Bash(bd:*) and Bash(git add:*) and the test-cmd entry; an explicit --allowed-tools value is passed through verbatim. npm detection case: temp project dir containing package.json with {\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"true\"}}, dry-run from that dir shows \"test gate: npm test\".","acceptance_criteria":"1. With no --allowed-tools flag, claude receives an allowlist containing Bash(bd:*), Bash(git add:*), Bash(git status:*), Bash(git diff:*), Bash(git log:*), Bash(git rev-parse:*), and Bash(\u003ctest_cmd\u003e:*) when a test gate is active. 2. An explicit --allowed-tools value (including empty) is passed verbatim. 3. A project with package.json scripts.test auto-detects \"npm test\" as the test gate without executing it during detection. 4. ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh passes.","notes":"CAUTION: unrelated in-flight work exists in the tree (export/digest files, ADR drafts). Stage ONLY scripts/bd-run-beads.py, scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh, and work-log.md; never git add -A/-u/. Quality gate: ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-14T03:09:29Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-14T03:25:16Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T03:27:01Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-y3l","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-daq","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T20:10:06Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-daq","title":"bd-run-beads: runner-side commit/close, dirty-tree guard, unattended prompt rewrite","description":"Context: a headless run in another repo (RankChoiceVoting) stalled: the session finished the work but git commit is not on any allowlist; headless -p cannot approve, the session ended without closing its bead, the close-gate FATALed and stranded the remaining 3 beads of the plan. Evidence: /home/stuar/proj/RankChoiceVoting/.bd-run-beads/20260714-024642Z/run.log lines 69-76. Fix: move privileged bookkeeping from the model session into the runner. All work is in scripts/bd-run-beads.py and scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh (fixture-driven bash test suite with fake bd and fake claude binaries; read it first).\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/bd-run-beads.py:\n1. session_prompt(): REMOVE the commit step and the close step. ADD an opening statement that the session runs unattended (headless; nobody can approve permission prompts or answer questions) and an explicit step: do not commit, do not push, do not close the bead - the runner commits and closes after its gates pass. Keep the claim, implement-only-this-issue, test, and work-log steps unchanged.\n2. Post-session flow (after rc==0 and the test gate passes): if the bead is already closed and the tree is unchanged, log and continue. Otherwise the runner itself runs git add -A (excluding the log dir via a pathspec like :(exclude)\u003crelpath\u003e ONLY when the log dir is inside the repo), then git commit -m \"\u003cbead title\u003e (\u003cbead id\u003e)\", then bd close \u003cbead id\u003e; verify with a fresh bd show that status == closed, else die.\n3. No-op guard: if the session made no file changes AND did not close the bead, die stating the session produced nothing, naming the bead and the transcript path.\n4. Dirty-tree guard: before running the first session, if git status --porcelain (log-dir entries excluded) is non-empty, die telling the user to commit or stash first or pass --allow-dirty. New flag --allow-dirty proceeds but logs a warning that pre-existing changes will be swept into the next bead commit.\n5. Update the module docstring to describe the new contract.\n\nCHANGES TO scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh:\n6. Fake bd: support close \u003cid\u003e (write closed to the status fixture file) and tolerate update subcommands; keep show as is.\n7. Fake claude: no longer closes the bead; instead it creates a marker file work-\u003cid\u003e.txt in cwd to simulate work, unless env NO_CHANGES=1.\n8. Execution cases must run inside a temp git repo: add helper mk_repo (git init -q, git config user.email/user.name, one initial commit).\n9. Rework case 6 into the no-op guard case (NO_CHANGES=1: run fails naming the bead). New assertions: after a successful run a commit exists whose message contains the bead id and the tree is clean; the bead status file reads closed (written by fake bd close, proving the runner invoked it); a dirty repo at start fails with guidance unless --allow-dirty is passed. Update the prompt-content assertions: the string \"Commit the changes\" no longer exists; the work-log ordering assertion should check the work-log step precedes the do-not-commit instruction.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Session prompt contains no commit/close instruction, states the session is unattended, and forbids commit/push/close. 2. After a successful bead: a git commit exists containing the bead id in its message, the working tree is clean, and the bead was closed by a runner-invoked bd close. 3. A session that changes nothing and does not close its bead fails the run with a message naming the bead. 4. Dirty tree at start fails with guidance unless --allow-dirty, which logs a sweep warning. 5. ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh passes.","notes":"CAUTION for the executing session: the working tree contains unrelated in-flight work (docs/DESIGN-export.md, docs/slack-ingestion.md, src/slackbackup/export*.py, tests/test_export_*.py, docs/adr/0002 and 0003 drafts). Stage ONLY the files this issue touches - scripts/bd-run-beads.py, scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh, and work-log.md. Never use git add -A, git add -u, or git add . in this repo. Verify with git status --short before committing that no export/digest files are staged. Quality gate for this issue is ./scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh (the repo pytest suite does not cover the runner).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-14T03:06:21Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-14T03:19:51Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T03:24:52Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-1cw","title":"Digest v3: real-archive verification + commit/close-out (sonnet-ok)","description":"Final step of the v3 change; all code/tests/docs are DONE and sit UNCOMMITTED in the working tree (320 tests green). This bead is pure verification + close-out, safe for a Sonnet session.\n\nCONTEXT: v3 = (a) condensation: posted_at_utc dropped, digest written compact via json.dumps(..., ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\",\":\")) in export.py _run_digest only (export_month/users_out stay indent=2); (b) top-level 'mentions' cross-workspace index (build_mentions_index in export_logic.py, deterministic identity unification via email_hash/normalized-F3-name, ambiguous never merged); (c) Block Kit mention/link extraction from blocks[].text.text (_block_texts in _clean, fixes SlackBackup-rie). _clean_user now emits email_hash (truncated sha256, raw email never persisted). Docs updated: DESIGN-export.md (v3 intro, sample JSON, §Mentions index, resolved-gaps rows), docs/adr/0002 + 0003 (both new, adr-quality-check passed), docs/slack-ingestion.md (v3 refs, identity guidance).\n\nSTEPS:\n1. .venv/bin/python -m pytest  — must be 320 passed.\n2. Regenerate real digests: ./slackbackup export digest --jobs \"jobs/*.json\" --archive-root ~/slack-backups  (takes minutes; f3-pugetsound job is the big one).\n3. Verify on ~/slack-exports/f3-pugetsound-digest-\u003ctoday\u003e.json:\n   - size ~15.7MB (v2 baseline 22.6MB at f3-pugetsound-digest-2026-07-13.json) — note the index adds some bytes over the pure-condensation estimate; record actual.\n   - json.load succeeds; schema_version == slack-llm-digest-v3; no posted_at_utc anywhere (spot-check messages[0] and a reply).\n   - top-level 'mentions' dict present and non-empty; entries have aliases/accounts/match_confidence/workspaces-\u003echannels-\u003emessage_ts; no message_url/text inside index.\n   - Block Kit fix: the f3kirkland ao-heritage-park backblast ts=1783887179.871339 ('Slurpee Day') must now carry mentions[] with ~14 \u003c@U...\u003e ids, and those PAX must appear in the mentions index pointing at C0A6DGHR7D3.\n   - users file: profiles carry email_hash, no raw email string anywhere (grep -c '@' sanity vs known-address absence).\n4. If any check fails: fix (small) or file a bead and stop before commit.\n5. Commit everything (tests, src, docs, ADRs, work-log) as one v3 commit referencing SlackBackup-1sx/vv0/du5/rie; close those four beads and this one; then session-completion protocol: git pull --rebase, bd dolt push, git push, git status must show up to date.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-14T02:50:40Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:51Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:51Z","close_reason":"Real-archive verification complete: schema_version v3, no posted_at_utc anywhere, mentions index well-formed (642 entries, 631 high / 11 ambiguous), Block Kit fix confirmed, zero raw emails across 13,087 profiles. Committed and pushed as cc5f2db.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-du5","title":"Digest v3: cross-workspace mention index (top-level mentions key)","description":"Folded into the uncommitted v3 change (SlackBackup-vv0/1sx) per user decision 2026-07-13: one schema change, schema_version stays slack-llm-digest-v3, index lives as a top-level 'mentions' key in the digest.\n\nGOAL: compact inverted index answering where/when a PAX is mentioned across workspaces, keyed by canonical F3 name, storing only message ts grouped by workspace-\u003echannel (counts/first-last/URLs derived downstream). No message bodies, no message URLs in the index.\n\nACs:\n1. Per-message raw \u003c@U...\u003e tokens and the existing per-message 'mentions' field are unchanged.\n2. User ids stay workspace-local; accounts listed as [workspace, user_id] pairs.\n3. Index keyed by canonical F3 name: handler's derived_leadership.possible_f3_name when present, else display_name, else real_name, else name. 'aliases' lists distinct raw forms encountered.\n4. Deterministic cross-workspace unification: (a) email_hash match -\u003e merge, confidence high; (b) normalized F3 name match (lowercase, strip non-alnum: case/space/punct/hyphen variants fold) + supporting evidence (matching normalized real_name or similar username) -\u003e high; (c) normalized name match with no contradicting evidence -\u003e medium.\n5. Conflict (same normalized name, differing email hashes AND differing real names) -\u003e no merge; one key with match_confidence 'ambiguous' and an 'identities' array of unmerged clusters.\n6. Structure per entry: {aliases, accounts, match_confidence, workspaces: {ws: {channels: {channel_id: {name, message_ts: [ts...]}}}}}; ts ascending; replies' mentions included; scoped to users actually mentioned in this digest.\n7. Email privacy: raw email never emitted anywhere; build_user_profiles gains profile.email_hash (truncated sha256 of lowercased email) as the only persisted evidence.\n8. manifest.counting_rules documents the index; DESIGN-export.md v3 section updated; new ADR-0003 records the identity-matching boundary revision (ADR-0001 left ALL merging to the LLM; v3 moves deterministic matching into the builder, ambiguity still flagged); docs/slack-ingestion.md identity guidance updated to match.\n9. Full suite green; real digest regen shows the index present and well-formed.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-14T02:40:57Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:43Z","started_at":"2026-07-14T02:41:12Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:43Z","close_reason":"Fully implemented and verified: mentions index built (deterministic email_hash/normalized-name unification, ambiguous conflicts flagged), email_hash added to user profiles, docs/ADR-0003/manifest updated, real f3-pugetsound digest regen confirms well-formed index (642 entries) with no PII leakage. Committed cc5f2db.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-vv0","title":"Digest v3: finish condensation integration — green phase, docs, ADR, verification","description":"Continuation of SlackBackup-1sx (analysis, ACs, and red-phase tests done). User decision on record: KEEP message_url (ADR-0001 rationale — LLM must never construct p\u003cts\u003e links; newsletter-prompt.md cites it). Condense via compact serialization + dropping posted_at_utc only.\n\nSTATE: red-phase test edits exist as UNCOMMITTED working-tree changes (3 tests failing, as intended):\n- tests/test_export_digest_logic.py ~315: schema_version == \"slack-llm-digest-v3\"; ~323-329: posted_at_utc absent from parent+reply, posted_at_local present; ~1125-1131: enrich test asserts no posted_at_utc.\n- tests/test_export_cli.py: new test_run_digest_writes_compact_json — file text must equal json.dumps(doc, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\",\":\")).\nIf the tree was reset, re-derive from those assertions.\n\nREMAINING (green phase):\n1. src/slackbackup/export_logic.py:\n   - _enrich_for_digest (~line 634): delete the posted_at_utc assignment; keep posted_at_local, message_url, and thread rollups. _format_utc stays (edited.at_utc, thread_last_reply_utc unchanged).\n   - build_digest (~line 982): schema_version -\u003e \"slack-llm-digest-v3\".\n   - manifest counting_rules: add \"posted_at_local\" note (DST-aware America/Los_Angeles, ISO-8601 with offset; UTC derivable from ts epoch or the offset; replaces v2's posted_at_utc).\n   - _channel_context docstring (~line 438): reword stale \"posted_at_utc convention\" reference.\n2. src/slackbackup/export.py:183 (_run_digest): out_path.write_text(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")), encoding=\"utf-8\"). Only the digest write — export_month (export_logic.py:267) and users_out (export.py:206,272) stay pretty-printed (possible follow-up bead for users_out, 5.9MB at indent=2).\n3. Docs:\n   - docs/DESIGN-export.md ~347-460: v2 -\u003e v3 intro (v3 is v2 minus posted_at_utc, compact-serialized), sample JSON drop posted_at_utc lines (408, 415, 421), prose at 439-440 (\"alongside posted_at_utc\"), resolved-limitations table (~566).\n   - New docs/adr/0002: v3 condensation decision (measured: whitespace 26% of file, posted_at_utc 1.0MB redundant; message_url deliberately retained). ADR-0001 is immutable — reference, do not edit. Run adr-quality-check before commit.\n   - docs/slack-ingestion.md lines 20-21, 44: v2 -\u003e v3, drop \"rather than converting posted_at_utc\" wording.\n4. Verify (AC5): .venv/bin/python -m pytest — full suite green including the 3 red tests. Then regenerate a real digest (./slackbackup export digest --jobs) and confirm ~15.7MB vs 22.6MB with parsed content identical minus posted_at_utc.\n5. Close SlackBackup-1sx and this bead together; per-field measurement script preserved at scratchpad digest_size_analysis.py pattern (rebuild trivially if gone).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T23:40:59Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:46Z","close_reason":"Green phase complete: condensation (compact JSON, posted_at_utc dropped), docs/ADR-0002, real digest verified 17.2MB vs 22.6MB baseline. Committed cc5f2db.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-1sx","title":"Digest v3: condense output — compact JSON, derived message_url, single local timestamp","description":"Digest v2 grew the f3-pugetsound digest 15.5MB -\u003e 22.6MB (+46%) with message count flat (+0.9%). Measured causes: pretty-print whitespace +2.8MB (indent=2 amplified by new nested arrays; overhead now 26% of file), posted_at_local +1.36MB, reactions +1.05MB, remaining v2 evidence fields +1.5MB.\n\nSCOPE DECISION (user, 2026-07-13): keep message_url — dropping it would reverse ADR-0001's rationale (LLM must never construct p\u003cts\u003e links) and newsletter-prompt.md cites from it. Condense via compact serialization + dropping the redundant UTC timestamp only.\n\nAC1: Digest JSON written compact (no indent). Parsed content unchanged except AC2.\nAC2: posted_at_utc removed from message/reply records; posted_at_local (DST-aware America/Los_Angeles offset, ISO-8601) retained — UTC remains derivable from ts (epoch) or the offset. thread_last_reply_utc and edited.at_utc unchanged. message_url kept.\nAC3: schema_version bumped to \"slack-llm-digest-v3\" (field removal breaks v2's additive contract — ADR-0001 explicitly promised v1 consumers keying on posted_at_utc keep working against v2). DESIGN-export.md updated; new ADR records the decision.\nAC4: Downstream prompt docs (docs/slack-ingestion.md) updated for v3 / posted_at_utc removal.\nAC5: Tests updated for v3 shape incl. compact-output test; full pytest suite passes.\n\nDone = digest for an unchanged archive parses to identical evidence minus posted_at_utc, file ~15.7MB vs 22.6MB (compact -5.9MB, utc -1.0MB), all ACs verified.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T23:21:22Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:47Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T23:21:26Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:47Z","close_reason":"Condensation implemented and verified against real archive regen. Committed cc5f2db.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-1sx","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-vv0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T16:41:03Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-rie","title":"Digest v2 mentions extraction misses Block Kit backblasts (PAX list lost)","description":"Bot-posted backblasts (F3 Nation/PAXminer crosspost, e.g. bot_id B0A3N3YRWE8) use Slack Block Kit: the top-level msg.text is an auto-generated narrative-only fallback with no PAX list, while the actual *PAX*: line with \u003c@U...\u003e mentions lives in blocks[0].text.text (a section block's mrkdwn). export_logic.py's _clean()/_extract_mentions() only ever reads msg[\"text\"] and never inspects msg[\"blocks\"], so for these bot-posted backblasts the digest's mentions[] is empty/wrong and the structured PAX participant list is silently lost - only the narrative survives. Confirmed on f3kirkland/ao-heritage-park ts=1783887179.871339 (\"Slurpee Day\", 2026-07-11): 14 \u003c@U...\u003e PAX mentions plus 4 plain-name PAX (Singlet, Van Winkle, The Dude, Welch's) exist only in blocks, not in text. Contrast with a plain human-typed backblast (no blocks, e.g. ts=1780770065.437219 \"Heritage Park x60\") where the PAX line is part of the top-level text and mentions[] extracts correctly. User confirms most backblasts in this deployment go through the bot tool (Block Kit), so this is the common case, not an edge case - a large fraction of backblasts across all AOs are likely missing structured PAX data in the digest right now.\n\n## Context\nDiscovered while investigating a user report that the f3pugetsound nightly digest showed the Slurpee Day (ao-heritage-park, f3kirkland) backblast as narrative-only with no PAX list. Root-caused via direct sqlite inspection (slack-backups/f3kirkland/ao-heritage-park/slackdump.sqlite) comparing the bot-posted message's blocks vs a plain human-typed backblast in the same channel. User confirms most backblasts across AOs are bot-posted (Block Kit), so this affects most channels, not just this one.","design":"Likely fix: in export_logic.py, add a helper that walks msg.get('blocks', []) for section blocks (block.get('text', {}).get('text')) and runs the existing _MENTION_RE over that text too, merging results into _extract_mentions()'s output (or a sibling call) before assigning base['mentions']. Should probably also apply the same treatment to _extract_links() if backblast blocks ever carry links. Needs a fixture derived from the real Slurpee Day message shape (top-level text = narrative fallback, blocks[0] = PAX section) added to scripts/test_fixtures/export-archive/ for regression coverage.","acceptance_criteria":"Given a bot-posted backblast message with a blocks[] section containing a *PAX*: line and one or more \u003c@U...\u003e mentions, when export_logic.py builds a digest entry for that message (_clean/_extract_mentions path, evidence=True), then the resulting mentions[] field includes every \u003c@U...\u003e user id found in the blocks section text, in addition to any found in the top-level text field (deduped, first-appearance order preserved across both sources).\n\nGiven a plain human-typed backblast with no blocks[] field, when the digest entry is built, then behavior is unchanged (mentions[] extracted from text as today).\n\nGiven a backblast (bot-posted or not) containing plain-text PAX entries with no Slack user id (e.g. 'Singlet', 'The Dude') that cannot be resolved to a \u003c@U...\u003e mention, when the digest entry is built, then those names remain visible via the raw text/blocks content (already true) - no requirement to resolve plain names to user ids.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T22:47:27Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:49Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T04:07:49Z","close_reason":"Block Kit blocks[].text.text extraction fixed; verified on real f3kirkland ao-heritage-park backblast (ts 1783887179.871339) now carries all 14 mentions. Committed cc5f2db.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-dbp","title":"bd-run-beads: prompt swallowed by --allowedTools; add per-run debug logging","description":"Two issues from the first real run: (1) the session prompt was passed as a positional arg after --allowedTools, which is variadic in the claude CLI, so it consumed the prompt and claude -p exited \"Input must be provided either through stdin or as a prompt argument when using --print\" - fix by writing the prompt to stdin; (2) a failed headless run left nothing to debug with - add a per-run log dir (--log-dir, default .bd-run-beads/, gitignored) holding run.log (plan, per-bead timings, git HEAD before/after, gate results) plus per-bead claude stream-json transcripts and stderr/test-gate output, with compact tool-call progress echoed to the console.","acceptance_criteria":"Prompt reaches the session via stdin (fake-claude test reads stdin); executed runs create run.log and \u003cbead\u003e.stream.jsonl; gate failures print the paths to the relevant logs; test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:48:25Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-13T17:51:53Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T17:51:53Z","close_reason":"stdin prompt delivery + per-run logging landed; real-CLI smoke test passed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-efk","title":"Digest v2: preserve reactions, edited, subtype, and unfurl evidence on digest messages","description":"Why: _clean() (src/slackbackup/export_logic.py ~line 67) reduces messages to ts/user/display_name/text/files, dropping evidence verified present in real archives: reactions (~20 percent of sampled messages - HC/confirmation signals), edited (~7 percent - corrections), subtype (thread_broadcast / channel_join / bot_message), and attachments - whose Slack message unfurls carry the quoted earlier message url/author/text, the only EXPLICIT cross-message reference evidence Slack records (key for \"message refers to an earlier message\" analysis).\n\nScope guard: export_month (monthly export) shares _clean(). Do NOT change monthly output in this bead - new fields would churn every sealed month file (the sealed-skip content comparison would rewrite them all). Add a keyword param _clean(msg, users_map, evidence=False) and pass evidence=True only from select_messages_in_range(). export_month keeps evidence=False.\n\nFields to add when evidence=True and the raw field is present (omit the key entirely when absent - no nulls):\n- reactions: [{name, count, users}] copied verbatim (user ids, not names).\n- edited: {user, at_utc} where at_utc converts the raw edited.ts via the existing _format_utc helper.\n- subtype: verbatim string.\n- unfurls: derived from raw attachments[]. For entries where is_msg_unfurl is true or from_url contains slack.com/archives/: emit {url: from_url, author_name, quoted_text: \u003cattachment text field\u003e, target_channel_id, target_ts}; parse targets from the /archives/\u003cCHANNEL\u003e/p\u003cdigits\u003e path (ts = digits with a dot inserted before the last 6 digits). For other attachments having from_url or title_link: emit {url, title}. Skip attachments with neither. Never modify the message text field itself.\n\nGuard: bot/system messages can lack user entirely (existing uid-None guard pattern - see bd memory slack-export-noise-fields).\n\nTests: one per new field with raw-message fixtures carrying it; unfurl target parsing (p1778086219226429 -\u003e ts 1778086219.226429); and monthly export output byte-identical for the existing fixtures (scripts/test_fixtures/export-archive).","acceptance_criteria":"Digest messages carry reactions/edited/subtype/unfurls exactly when the raw archive data has them; a pasted Slack permalink surfaces target_channel_id/target_ts on an unfurl entry; monthly export output is unchanged; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:11:25Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T18:41:30Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T18:42:53Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-efk","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-7jn","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T10:11:45Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-7jn","title":"Digest v2: include threads whose replies fall in scope (fix cross-period thread blindness)","description":"Why: select_messages_in_range() in src/slackbackup/export_logic.py (~line 471) admits a thread only when the PARENT ts is inside [from_epoch, to_epoch]. A thread parented before the export window that received replies inside the window is entirely absent from the digest, so revived/long-running conversations vanish. The monthly exporter already handles the analogous case (late reply reopens a sealed month, see docs/DESIGN-export.md Idempotency); the digest never did.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. In select_messages_in_range(), include a thread when the parent OR at least one reply has ts in range. When only replies are in range, emit the full thread (parent + all replies, same nesting as today) but set \"in_scope\": false on the parent record. Records without the flag are implicitly in scope; never emit in_scope: true (size).\n2. _channel_activity() (~line 538) must exclude in_scope:false parents from root_message_count, participant sets, and first/last message timestamps; their nested replies still count exactly as replies do today (total = root + reply unchanged). This keeps every v1 count meaning identical for previously included threads.\n3. Bump schema_version to slack-llm-digest-v2 in build_digest() and add a manifest.counting_rules entry documenting in_scope semantics.\n4. _enrich_for_digest already recurses into replies; the out-of-scope parent must still get message_url/posted_at_utc and thread rollup fields like any parent.\n\nTests (tests/test_export_digest_logic.py, follow the existing fake convert_fn fixture pattern, e.g. test_build_digest_merges_across_workspaces_chronologically):\n- parent before window + reply inside: thread present; parent has in_scope false; root_message_count excludes the parent; the reply is counted; participant_count excludes the parent author unless that author also has an in-scope record.\n- parent and replies inside window: no in_scope key anywhere (v1 behavior unchanged).\n- parent and all replies before window: thread absent (unchanged).","acceptance_criteria":"A 180-day digest includes a thread parented 200 days ago with a reply 5 days ago; the parent is flagged in_scope:false and excluded from all activity counts; schema_version reads slack-llm-digest-v2; counting_rules documents in_scope; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:11:22Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T17:57:18Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T18:39:35Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":6,"comment_count":0}
