{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-a70","title":"export_transform.sh: jq ARG_MAX failure on months with many messages","description":"## Steps to Reproduce\nRun scripts/export-monthly.sh against a real archive whose target month has enough\nmessages that the per-month transformed JSON exceeds the OS command-line length\nlimit, e.g.:\n  ./scripts/export-monthly.sh --from 2026-01-01 --to 2026-06-22 \\\n    --workspace f3pugetsound --channel classifieds \\\n    --archive-root ~/slack-backups --out ~/slack-exports\n\n## What happened\nexport_transform.sh line 134 passed the full per-month $messages JSON via\n'jq --argjson', which exceeds the OS command-line length limit ('jq: Argument list\ntoo long') once a month has enough messages. Hit in production on 3 of 15 tracked\nchannels (dungeons-of-finn-hill/ai-coding, f3cascades/all-f3-cascades,\nf3pugetsound/classifieds) during the 2026-06-22 backup+export run.\n\nWorse, bash's '\u003e $target' redirect still created the output file before jq failed,\nleaving a corrupt 0-byte file that a later idempotent re-run treated as\nalready-written and skipped (since the month was already sealed by the high-water\nmark) — silently leaving permanently-missing data unless someone notices the\n0-byte file.","design":"Fixed by writing $messages to a temp file and passing it via 'jq --slurpfile messages \u003cfile\u003e' (indexing $messages[0]) instead of --argjson on the command line. Re-ran scripts/test_export_monthly.sh (all pass) and re-exported the 3 affected channels after deleting their corrupt 2026-04 files.","acceptance_criteria":"export-monthly.sh succeeds end-to-end on all 15 tracked channels with no zero-byte output files; scripts/test_export_monthly.sh passes.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-06-22T20:28:41Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-06-22T20:28:53Z","closed_at":"2026-06-22T20:28:53Z","close_reason":"Fixed in scripts/lib/export_transform.sh: switched to --slurpfile via temp file instead of --argjson on the command line. Verified via scripts/test_export_monthly.sh (all pass) and a full re-export of all 15 tracked channels (47 output files, none empty).","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-d3r","title":"Spike: evaluate slackdump native resume vs custom last_ts.txt logic","description":"P1 design gap from review: scripts/incremental-dump.sh + last_ts.txt reimplements logic slackdump already provides natively (resuming a previous archive, adding only new messages). Determine whether slackdump's native resume mode satisfies UC-1 (incremental backup) and UC-2 (full re-sync ignoring prior state) as-is.","acceptance_criteria":"Decision recorded: either (a) native resume satisfies UC-1/UC-2 and SlackBackup-4i2 is closed/superseded with scripts/bej/90o simplified to drop custom timestamp tracking, or (b) native resume is insufficient and the specific gap it leaves is documented as the justification for keeping custom logic.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-06-21T03:14:57Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-06-21T04:33:07Z","closed_at":"2026-06-21T05:12:50Z","close_reason":"Native resume confirmed viable for UC-1/UC-2 (drop custom last_ts.txt logic in favor of archive+resume). But -dedupe flag has a confirmed data-loss bug: it deletes thread-root (IS_PARENT=1) message rows, verified by diffing a resume+dedupe archive against an independent fresh archive of the same channel (helpdesk, f3pugetsound workspace) - 9/9 thread parents missing. Decision: use resume WITHOUT -dedupe; accept duplicate rows across cycles rather than risk silent loss of thread metadata. Consider filing upstream with rusq/slackdump.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
