{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-tct","title":"bd-run-beads: worker sessions append a work-log entry via the work-log skill","description":"After notable work the project work-log should be updated via the work-log skill. Integration point: the worker session itself (not the runner, not a separate logger session) invokes /work-log, because (a) a bead session is single-objective with an explicitly stated goal, exactly the case where the skill v3 rules skip the confirmation gate, (b) the skill captures the session id mechanically from the most-recent transcript, which for the worker IS the session that did the work - audit pairing stays intact - and (c) the worker knows the real rationale/outcomes, not a paraphrase. The step runs BEFORE the commit step so work-log.md lands inside the bead commit instead of accumulating dirty across beads. Runner side: --work-log auto|on|off (auto = enabled when a work-log skill dir exists user- or project-level); when enabled, warn in run.log (never fail) if work-log.md did not grow during a bead.","acceptance_criteria":"Prompt contains the work-log step exactly when enabled; step precedes commit; runner warns (not dies) when work-log.md unchanged; --work-log off restores old prompt; tests cover on/off and the warning path.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T19:06:04Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-13T19:08:41Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T19:08:41Z","close_reason":"prompt step reusing /work-log + warn-only capture check landed; 30 test assertions green","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-j7b","title":"General-purpose bead-runner script: dependency-ordered headless claude sessions with model cues","description":"A reusable script (scripts/bd-run-beads.sh) that takes one or more target bead ids, resolves their transitive open blocks-dependencies via bd show --json into dependency-first execution order (deduped, cycle-detected), chooses a model per bead from cues - label model:\u003cname\u003e wins over a [\u003cmodel\u003e] or [\u003cmodel\u003e-ok] tag in the title, falling back to a --default-model (sonnet) - and runs one headless claude -p session per bead sequentially. After each session it enforces hard gates: the project test command passes and the bead status is closed, stopping on first failure. Skips already-closed beads so reruns are restartable. --dry-run prints the plan (order, model, cue source) without executing. Project-agnostic: test command auto-detected (.venv/bin/pytest, then pytest if pyproject.toml) and overridable via --test-cmd; bd/claude binaries overridable via BD_BIN/CLAUDE_BIN for testing. Companion scripts/test_bd_run_beads.sh uses PATH-shimmed fake bd/claude fixtures, matching the repo test_*.sh convention.","acceptance_criteria":"Dry-run over SlackBackup-tdq prints all 7 digest-v2 beads dependency-first with correct models (s1n/lwx haiku, rest sonnet); label model:\u003cx\u003e overrides a title cue; closed beads skipped; a dependency cycle aborts with a clear error; a session that leaves the bead unclosed or tests failing stops the run non-zero; test_bd_run_beads.sh passes.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:25:26Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-13T17:29:49Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T17:26:03Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T17:29:49Z","close_reason":"scripts/bd-run-beads.sh + test suite landed; dry-run verified against the real digest-v2 tree","dependency_