{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-ugs","title":"Digest v2: mentions/links extraction and per-workspace user_index","description":"Why: message text keeps raw Slack tokens. \u003c@U123\u003e mentions are unresolvable inside the digest (no id-to-name map ships with it) and \u003curl|label\u003e links need parsing. Deterministic extraction only - the text field is never modified.\n\nWhat (src/slackbackup/export_logic.py, digest path only - reuse the evidence=True seam from the reactions bead if it has landed):\n1. mentions: parse text for \u003c@U[A-Z0-9]+\u003e tokens; emit mentions: [ids] in order of first appearance, deduped; omit the key when empty. Applies to every message and reply.\n2. links: parse Slack angle-bracket tokens \u003curl\u003e and \u003curl|label\u003e where url starts with http; emit links: [{url, label (null for bare urls), type}] with type = slack_message when the url matches slack.com/archives/\u003cC-id\u003e/p\u003cdigits\u003e (also add target_channel_id and target_ts, parsed the same way as the unfurl bead: dot before last 6 digits), slack_file when the url contains slack.com/docs/ or slack.com/files/, else external. Ignore non-url tokens (\u003c@U...\u003e, \u003c#C...\u003e, \u003c!here\u003e). Omit the key when empty.\n3. user_index: new top-level digest section {workspace: {user_id: {display_name, is_bot}}} built from the profiles_doc already loaded in build_digest(). Include ONLY ids actually referenced in that workspace slice of the digest: message/reply authors, mentions, reactions users, channel creators, file creators. This bounds size and stays workspace-scoped - it is NOT the rejected cross-workspace merged identity table; update the build_digest docstring sentence about author identity so it stays accurate, and state the non-merge rule in the manifest.\n4. Document mentions/links/user_index in the manifest (counting_rules or a new enrichment note).\n\nTests: mention order + dedupe; bare vs labeled links; a slack_message link yields target_channel_id/target_ts; user_index contains a mentioned-but-never-posting user and excludes an unreferenced roster user; two workspaces with the same user id stay under separate workspace keys with their own display names.","acceptance_criteria":"mentions/links appear exactly when tokens exist and text is byte-identical to raw; user_index is per-workspace, referenced-ids-only; manifest documents the enrichment; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:11:30Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T18:51:41Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T18:55:33Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-ugs","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-7jn","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T10:11:51Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-lwx","title":"[haiku-ok] Digest v2: channel_url, message-file ids, and message anchors on channel files","description":"Three small additive joins in src/slackbackup/export_logic.py:\n1. channel_url: in build_digest(), every channels[] entry (both ok and missing_archive) gets channel_url = https://\u003cworkspace\u003e.slack.com/archives/\u003cchannel_id\u003e. Add a digest_channel_url() helper next to digest_message_url() (~line 327), same style.\n2. Message-level files: the _clean() files projection (~line 74) additionally keeps id: f.get(\"id\"), so a message-attached file joins to the channel-level files list (which already carries id).\n3. Channel-level files: _load_channel_files() (~line 426) currently does SELECT DATA FROM FILE. Change to SELECT DATA, MESSAGE_ID FROM FILE and emit message_ts on the cleaned entry when MESSAGE_ID is non-null (null means a standalone channel Canvas - see bd memory slackdump-canvas-is-just-a-file). FIRST verify against a real archive (read-only sqlite query on any ~/slack-backups/\u003cws\u003e/\u003cch\u003e/slackdump.sqlite that has a message-attached file) that MESSAGE_ID holds the message ts string; if it is a different key, name the field message_id instead and record what it joins to in a code comment. Dedupe-by-id keeps the last row seen today; when merging duplicate rows prefer one with non-null MESSAGE_ID over null.\n\nTests: channel_url present on every channel entry including missing_archive; message file entries carry id; a FILE row with MESSAGE_ID set surfaces message_ts while a channel-canvas row (null MESSAGE_ID) has no such key; duplicate FILE rows where only one has MESSAGE_ID resolve to the anchored one.","acceptance_criteria":"All three fields present per description; the MESSAGE_ID meaning was verified against a real archive before naming the output field; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stu