{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-4ao","title":"Digest v2: per-channel seq giving deterministic flat chronological order","description":"Why: digest messages nest replies under parents and sort top-level entries by root ts, so the true channel timeline (what the channel looked like when a later top-level continuation was posted) is not directly readable. A per-channel monotonic sequence number gives a deterministic flat reconstruction without duplicating records - core to letting a downstream LLM infer relationships between top-level continuation messages.\n\nWhat: in build_digest() (src/slackbackup/export_logic.py, inside the per-channel loop, after select_messages_in_range and _enrich_for_digest), flatten that channel's emitted records (every root plus every nested reply), sort ascending by float(ts) (Slack ts are unique per channel; tie-break by the ts string for determinism), and assign seq = 1..N as an int field on each record dict (mutating the dicts updates them in place inside the nesting - nesting itself is untouched).\n\nSemantics to document in manifest.counting_rules: seq orders all records PRESENT in the digest for that channel (per channel, not global; roots and replies interleaved by true post time); no gaps; records outside the export window are simply not numbered.\n\nTests: root A (t1), reply A1 (t3), root B (t2) -\u003e seq A=1, B=2, A1=3 (a reply posted after a later root sorts after it); two channels each start at seq 1; an out-of-window reply under an in-scope parent still gets a seq consistent with its ts.","acceptance_criteria":"Every message and reply carries an integer seq; sorting one channel's records by seq equals sorting the flattened set by float(ts); seq semantics documented in counting_rules; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:11:28Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T18:39:54Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T18:41:01Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-4ao","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-7jn","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T10:11:48Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-s1n","title":"[haiku-ok] Digest v2: thread_ts on replies and Pacific-local timestamps","description":"Two mechanical additive fields in src/slackbackup/export_logic.py _enrich_for_digest() (~line 507):\n1. Every nested reply gets thread_ts set to its parent message ts. Pass the parent ts into the recursive _enrich_for_digest call for replies (root messages must NOT get a thread_ts field). This makes a reply record self-describing when an LLM extracts it away from its nesting.\n2. Every message AND reply gets posted_at_local next to posted_at_utc: ISO-8601 with offset in America/Los_Angeles via zoneinfo (stdlib), e.g. 2026-06-17T08:12:00-07:00, derived from float(ts) the same way posted_at_utc is.\nNote: _enrich_for_digest recurses into replies; replies have no replies key so the rollup branch is already skipped - keep it that way.\n\nTests in tests/test_export_digest_logic.py: a reply carries thread_ts equal to its parent ts plus its own posted_at_local; the parent has posted_at_local and no thread_ts; DST edge - one ts in January renders -08:00 and one in July renders -07:00.","acceptance_criteria":"All digest messages and replies carry posted_at_local (America/Los_Angeles, correct DST offset); every reply carries thread_ts == parent ts; roots have no thread_ts; full test suite passes.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Stuart Donaldson","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-07-13T17:11:26Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:56:15Z","started_at":"2026-07-13T18:48:34Z","closed_at":"2026-07-13T18:50:48Z","close_reason":"Closed","labels":["model:haiku"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"SlackBackup-s1n","depends_on_id":"SlackBackup-7jn","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-13T10:11:47Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
