{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-c8r","title":"search-messages.sh: cross-workspace message search to HTML report","description":"New capability, not part of the original DESIGN-files.md scope: search for\nmessages (not files) across every registered f3* workspace and render\nresults as one HTML page, most recent first, each linking to its channel\nand to the message itself in Slack.\n\nImplemented: scripts/search-messages.sh, scripts/lib/message_search_helpers.sh.\nReuses scripts/lib/fetch_files_helpers.sh's candidate_f3_workspaces/\nis_workspace_registered (same f3*-workspace-loop pattern as fetch-files.sh).\n\nSEARCH_MESSAGE already carries CHANNEL_ID, CHANNEL_NAME, TS, TXT, and the\nDATA blob has a ready permalink - no channel-catalog lookup needed (unlike\nbuild-file-index.sh's handling of `search files`' CHANNEL_ID=\"SEARCH\"\nplaceholder).\n\nFound and fixed two real HTML-escaping bugs against live data:\n1. Double-escaping: Slack's TXT column already HTML-entity-escapes bare \"\u0026\"\n   (e.g. \"PB\u0026amp;J\") per Slack's documented formatting convention; naively\n   applying jq's @html again produced \"\u0026amp;amp;\". Fixed by decoding\n   \u0026lt;/\u0026gt;/\u0026amp; back to raw characters first, then escaping once.\n2. Unescaped mention/link syntax: Slack's own \u003c@U..|name\u003e/\u003c#C..\u003e/\u003curl|label\u003e\n   syntax uses literal, unescaped angle brackets (that's syntax, not HTML) -\n   embedding it raw risks the browser treating it as a bogus tag and\n   silently dropping the content. Fixed by escaping the decoded text\n   uniformly, so mentions render as safe literal text\n   (e.g. \"\u0026lt;@U123|name\u0026gt;\") instead of vanishing or rendering unsafely.\n\n12 passing tests (scripts/test_search_messages.sh), verified live against\nall registered f3* workspaces (122 real results, correct sort order,\ncorrect escaping, no unregistered-workspace failures).","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Stuart Do