{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-2pd","title":"export digest: most_active_human_channel missed bot posting as ordinary user account","description":"Found via real-data verification of SlackBackup-fjw: f3kirkland's nation_bot_logs bot posts as user U0A3GF12LEA (roster is_bot=true), not via Slack's legacy bot_id field, so the original B-id-prefix-only heuristic in _is_bot_author didn't exclude it from most_active_human_channel. Fixed in the same session by also consulting the workspace roster's is_bot flag (build_user_profiles, moved earlier in build_digest to compute bot_ids_by_workspace before the per-channel activity pass). Added regression test test_build_digest_most_active_human_channel_excludes_bot_posting_as_ordinary_user. Closing as already fixed.","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-06-25T03:31:44Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-06-25T03:32:04Z","closed_at":"2026-06-25T03:32:04Z","close_reason":"Fixed: bot detection now also checks the workspace roster's is_bot flag (not just B-id-prefix), via bot_ids_by_workspace built from build_user_profiles before the per-channel activity pass. Regression test added. 209/209 tests pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"SlackBackup-8ew","title":"all-pax (f3pugetsound) archives with 0 messages despite 1830 members","description":"slackdump archive -o \u003cdir\u003e C77PPNCUT completes successfully (chunk #10, type MESSAGES, final=1) but with num_rec=0 - the Slack API returned zero messages for this channel, confirmed reproducible (re-archived from scratch twice with identical result). Not a corruption/bug in the SlackBackup tooling (bash or Python) - the archive command itself reports success with a complete, empty MESSAGES chunk. all-pax is the workspace's renamed 'general' channel (previous_names: ['general'], is_general: true), posting restricted to admins per its channel purpose. Hypothesis: a permissions/scope issue specific to this channel for the current session token, not a tooling bug. Needs investigation with a fresh session cookie or by checking Slack admin-side channel history settings - not actionable from this codebase alone.","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"stuart.donaldson@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-06-23T20:46:06Z","created_by":"Stuart Donaldson","updated_at":"2026-07-12T04:45:30Z","closed_at":"2026-07-12T04:45:30Z","close_reason":"Rejected as not actionable in this codebase. Root cause is external: Slack API returns 0 messages for all-pax (renamed 'general', admin-restricted) for the current session token — a permissions/history-visibility issue, not tooling. The tooling-side consequence (resume cannot continue from a 0-message archive) already has a shipped workaround: backup_logic wipes and re-archives 0-message dirs (see comment citing this issue). Nothing further to build; re-open only if a fresh cookie/admin-history check shows the tooling mishandling a channel that DOES return messages.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
